$ ----------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Small stationary SWAN test that exercises the quasi-coherent (GEN4/QCM)
$ path added for the quasi-coherent regression.
$
$ Identical to the two-cases mini deck apart from GEN4: IQCM=1 activates
$ QCSOURCE, which calls SWQCDFT/SWQCUFT/SWQCWIG. Those three read the
$ threadprivate stencil in the pre-B1 code and receive it explicitly now.
$ ----------------------------------------------------------------------

PROJECT 'QCMREF' '001'
SET NAUTICAL
MODE STATIONARY TWODIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN

$ Computational grid: 4 x 2 meshes (5 x 3 points).
$ Spectral grid: 8 directions and 12 frequencies from 0.05 to 1.0 Hz.
CGRID REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 2000.0 1000.0 4 2 CIRCLE 12 0.05 1.0 8

$ A 2 x 2 input grid is sufficient for the spatially constant 20 m depth.
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 1 1 2000.0 1000.0
READINP BOTTOM 1.0 'bottom.bot' 3 0 FREE

$ Uniform 8 m/s wind and a 1 m, 6 s JONSWAP spectrum enter from the west.
WIND 8.0 270.0
BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDSPEC SIDE WEST CONSTANT PAR 1.0 6.0 270.0 20.0

$ GEN4 activates the quasi-coherent scattering (IQCM=1); keep the breaking
$ and friction choices explicit so default changes do not alter the test.
GEN4
NUMERIC STOPC STAT 2
BREAKING CONSTANT 1.0 0.73
FRICTION JONSWAP CONSTANT 0.038

$ A single easy-to-inspect value at the domain centre.
POINTS 'CENTER' 1000.0 500.0
TABLE 'CENTER' HEADER 'qcm_center.tbl' XP YP DEPTH HSIGN TM01 DIR

COMPUTE
STOP
